  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). A browser-only, GeneDoc-style alignment viewer and editor. You can shade and edit alignments, realign blocks with MAFFT or MACSE, translate and check codons, cluster rows into subfamilies, find motifs and repeats, draw dot plots and build trees, then export SVG, RTF, FASTA or Newick. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
